Runtime: do not abort when /proc/self/exe cannot be read.

What: _swift_initRuntimePath (static linking: dladdr() returns nothing) retries
readlink("/proc/self/exe"), then falls back to getauxval(AT_EXECFN) and finally
program_invocation_name / PATH; if everything fails the runtime path is null
instead of fatalError("Unable to obtain Swift runtime path").
Why: on iSH readlink("/proc/self/exe") fails intermittently; every program that
touched the concurrency runtime aborted in ~95% of runs.
Upstream: likely acceptable (the only consumer already tolerates a null path).

Apply inside the `swift` repository: git apply <this file>
---
